\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Govt Sees 2001 Fiscal Deficit At 6% GDP \b0\par\par\uc2 578 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 August 2001\par 17:58\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian government forecasts that the country's fiscal deficit will grow to 6% of gross domestic product this year from 4.5% in 2000, as regional turmoil sent interest rates soaring and weakened the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  sharply in recent months. \par \par \uc2  Addressing investors in a conference call Wednesday, Finance Ministry Executive Secretary Amaury Bier also said next year's fiscal deficit is expected to fall to 4.05% of GDP. \par \par \uc2  He said the forecast, which is included in the recently inked $15 billion loan program with the International Monetary Fund, is based on a set of interest-rate and exchange-rate assumptions that wasn't disclosed. \par \par \uc2  Under the new IMF agreement, the details of which were unveiled Tuesday, Brazil raised its primary budget surplus target - which excludes debt servicing costs - to 3.35% of GDP this year and 3.5% in 2002, from 3% previously. The surplus aims to keep Brazil's public debt burden from growing. \par \par \uc2  Bier said the federal government will be responsible for the bulk of the 2002 primary budget surplus target, contributing 2.8% of GDP to the 3.5% target. \par \par \uc2  Regional governments and the companies they control are expected to contribute the remaining 0.7% of GDP. \par \par \uc2  With the surplus, the government expects Brazil's net public debt to rise to 53.95% of GDP at the end of 2001, from 49.5% at the end of last year. \par \par \uc2  By the end of 2002, the net debt burden is seen at 53.22% of GDP and headed toward a "very clear downward trend," said Bier during the conference sponsored by Salomon Smith Barney. \par \par \uc2  He said the estimate takes into account a plan to recognize hidden public-sector liabilities totaling 0.8% of GDP between this year and next and is net of any privatization revenues. \par \par \uc2  Bier declined to say which state-owned assets are listed for sale. \par \par \uc2  He said the new tax on fuels, which is being debated by lawmakers for approval, is expected to generate revenue of some BRR4 billion annually. The new tax will replace the so-called oil account as of 2002, which is an indirect tax on fuel. \par \par \uc2  Even though the IMF has revised Brazil's end-2001 inflation target to 5.8% from 4%, \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  director for economic research Ilan Goldfajn stressed that the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  will continue to pursue the government-set 4% goal. \par \par \uc2  As a result, the new IMF target won't affect the handling of monetary policy, Goldfajn said. He added that the new IMF target was just a "more realistic" forecast for inflation this year, since the Brazilian economy went through many shocks, such as the energy crisis and a weak \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . Goldfajn noted that the IMF and government's inflation targets converge to 3.5% at the end of 2002. \par \par \uc2  Market consensus is that inflation will be 6.2% \par \par \uc2  Goldfajn said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  expects to see the country's net international reserves at $28 billion at the end of the year. \par \par \uc2  This means that \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  can spend up to $8 billion on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , if needed. \par \par \uc2  He also said the $28-billion figure doesn't take into account new possible loans from the Inter-American Development Bank and World Bank that Brazil is currently negotiating. \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11 3145-1481; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010808dx88000yx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
