\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Ends Stronger On New IMF Deal,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 286 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 August 2001\par 22:55\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2  (Copyright (c) 2001, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.) \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended stronger Monday on a new agreement with the International Monetary Fund for $15 billion and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the battered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Gains, however, were muted as the market continued to fret about a possible debt default in Argentina, where the IMF said Friday it would accelerate a $1.2 billion disbursement needed to help keep the country solvent. \par \par \uc2  Doubts remain about whether Brazil's IMF deal would be enough to fend off the likely heavy contagion that a potential rupture in Argentina would bring, traders said. \par \par \uc2  A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  also added to the real's gains. "They (the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  today, but it's getting harder to see how much effect they are having because they are doing it more quietly," said a trader in Rio de Janeiro. \par \par \uc2  Since late June, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling about $50 million daily after earmarking $6 billion for the rest of the year to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the spot market and contain the weakening of the real, which has slipped by over 20% this year. \par \par \uc2  Signs indicate \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  may continue. Reports have said the IMF has agreed to give \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  added room to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the real, by reducing the country's foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reserve floor to about $20 billion from $25 billion. Reserves currently sit at about $35 billion. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at BRR2.460 to the dollar on a spread of BRR2.459-BRR2.461 spread. On Friday, the real closed at BRR2.505 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010806dx860016u\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
