\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil Real Ends Weaker, Despite Ctrl Bk Moves,Rate Hike \b0\par\par\uc2 278 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 Juli 2001\par 22:40\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and an interest-rate hike, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real succumbed to gravity yet again and finished weaker Thursday. \par \par \uc2  The real closed at a midrate of BRR2.508 on a spread of BRR2.507 to BRR2.509 a day after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by 75 basis points to 19%. \par \par \uc2  This compares with the real's finish of BRR2.500 Wednesday when it also weakened, despite \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  efforts to rescue it by selling dollars in the market. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is losing value after fears of an economic meltdown in Argentina resurfaced. The real posted gains Tuesday when the Argentine government late Monday announced it had clinched political backing for a deficit-cutting plan. \par \par \uc2  However, investors now fear that such measures won't be enough to avert a default in debt, traders said. \par \par \uc2  At the start Thursday, the real weakened to as much as BRR2.535, prompting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to sell dollars - a move that was confirmed by the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  at the end of the session. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the early decline partly stemmed from concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't move in favor of a bigger rate hike. The market was expecting the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to raise interest rates by 50 to 175 basis points to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , help stave off possible contagion from Argentina and curb inflation. A Dow Jones Newswires survey of 14 financial institutions this week generated a consensus forecast of a 150-basis point increase. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020010719dx7j00f4i\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
