\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends Stronger On Argentina,  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 301 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2001\par 23:09\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real ended sharply stronger Tuesday after an early \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  got a bounce from Argentine President Fernando de la Rua's clinching of political support for deficit-cutting plan. \par \par \uc2  Expectations of a hike in Brazil's basic interest rate Wednesday added to the strengthening, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real ended at a midrate of BRR2.498 per dollar on a wide spread of BRR2.496-BRR2.500. \par \par \uc2  Monday the real closed at BRR2.581, after uncertainties about De la Rua's negotiating skills with opposition parties forced the real beyond BRR2.60, setting a new record for weakness. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's early \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a big impact (on the real) because of Argentina's political developments," said a Sao Paulo trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of not confirming \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , but the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling dollars daily on the market to prop up the real for about the last two weeks as part of a $6 billion plan to protect its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Market players, said although De la Rua has mustered the support of Peronist governors to make spending cuts needed to pay debts, it remains to be seen if the cuts will be big enough or if Argentina's economy can be turned around. \par \par \uc2  A Dow Jones Newswires survey of 14 economists forecasts Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will hike its basic interest rate between 50 and 675 basis points Wednesday. The basic rate is currently at 18.25%. \par \par \uc2  Rating agency Fitch's announcement Tuesday that it changed Brazil's credit outlook for its sovereign rating to negative from stable had little impact on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  -Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020010717dx7h00hld\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
