\par\par \b \uc2  Brazil real ends at new low on Argentina woes. \b0\par\par\uc2 219 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Juli 2001\par 23:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, July 10 (Reuters) - Brazil's real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  slumped 1.7 percent to a new record low close on Tuesday amid fresh market concerns on Argentina and despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to shore up the real with market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 , traders said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  closed at 2.492 per greenback compared to Monday's close of 2.45, sinking below than its previous all-time low close of 2.48 on June 19. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  failed to stop the real's slide as a key Treasury auction late in the day in neighboring Argentina disappointed investors and added to worries about the country's fiscal solvency. \par \par \uc2  "The negative reaction should continue into trading tomorrow," said Luiz Rabi, chief economist at BicBanco. \par \par \uc2  Argentina was forced to pay relatively high rates to place short-term debt on Tuesday, fanning fears the country may have trouble making payments on its $128 billion public debt. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, selling dollars on Tuesday for the fifth time this month. Traders said that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is likely holding back some ammunition, however, in case the turbulence in Argentina worsens. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is practically the only seller (of dollars) in the market," Rabi said. \par 