\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 2-Battered  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real bounces on  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2  By Nicholas Winning \par \uc2 560 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Juli 2001\par 22:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 , July 6 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real ended firmer on Friday after a yo-yo session in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  as it clawed its way back from an Argentine-inspired record low. \par \par \uc2  The real firmed to close at 2.435 per dollar, still 24.8 percent weaker on the year, after hitting a record low of 2.560 per dollar earlier on concerns about Argentina's economic problems. It closed at 2.470 per dollar on Thursday. \par \par \uc2  "First it (the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) asked about the spread and then it sold a bit," one trader said. Two other dealers said the bank sold dollars. \par \par \uc2  The bank confirmed the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  but, as is its custom, gave no details about how it acted. It was the third confirmation of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from the bank this week. \par \par \uc2  Traders had expected the bank to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  late in the session to take advantage of expected thinner liquidity ahead of a partial market holiday on Monday. \par \par \uc2  On Thursday, the bank said it would spend $6 billion in the market this year to bolster the beleaguered \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The figure impressed few, however, as in the past few weeks the bank fed $1.7 billion to the dollar-hungry market. \par \par \uc2  The real has dropped like a stone this year on a heady mix of worries about fallout from Argentina's economic problems, the U.S. economic slowdown, and emergency energy rationing and political scandals at home. \par \par \uc2  The Argentine concerns heightened this week as investors feared the country's government would lose cross-party support for measures to end three years of economic stagnation. The latest bout of Argentine political tension was over a federal government spat with the opposition about provincial spending. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 CENTRAL BANK\b0 \highlight\uc2  UNDER FIRE \par \par \uc2  Players said the weakness of the real and the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to support it were casting an ever darker cloud over the performance of Latin America's biggest economy. \par \par \uc2  "I'm looking at economic activity slowing down faster than I thought, looking at \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  crashing, an outlook for even higher interest rates and I'm scared," said one economist who did not want to be identified. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new effort to support the real and prevent its seemingly interminable slide from fueling inflation with higher interest rates and regular market \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  has yet to break the trend. \par \par \uc2  Some Wall Street players mulled the thought that the Bank may choose to raise interest rates to bolster the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  instead of lining speculators pockets by backing it with cash. \par \par \uc2  Some economists argue that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's stance, especially Thursday's announcement of how much it would spend to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , was tantamount to making itself a sitting duck for speculators. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  invited a speculative attack by showing its threshold for pain," BCP Securities Latin American economist Walter Molano said in his daily note. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  must decide whether or not it has a floating exchange rate regime. Otherwise, it will lose control of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," he said. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga defended himself from criticism in Friday's edition of the daily newspaper Estado de S. Paulo. "The rule is to be transparent and that's what we are doing," Fraga told Estado columnist Sonia Racy. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010706dx76004bn\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
