\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's real weakens despite CenBank  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 279 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Juli 2001\par 23:08\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, July 3 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  weakened on Tuesday despite attempts by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to buttress its real as renewed worries over neighboring Argentina's political and economic problems rocked the market. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold greenbacks on Tuesday and the bank confirmed an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , although it did not specify what kind. But the helping hand was not enough to counteract the impact of new political jitters in Argentina. \par \par \uc2  The real still finished near its lowest point in the day at 2.353 reais per U.S. dollar, its third straight decline and a 0.90 percent depreciation from Monday's closing price. It is about 20 percent lower on the year. \par \par \uc2  Turnover was thin ahead of the U.S. Independence Day holiday on Wednesday, traders said. \par \par \uc2  "The market has an eye on Argentina," said a trader at a Sao Paulo bank. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's on-going failure to kick-start its economy out of a three-year recession has helped chip away at the real's worth all year as investors in Brazil worry its neighbors' woes may further roil its own economy. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has recovered from its all-time low of 2.48 last month - a 27 percent slide in the year - after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  announced it would aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Although Argentine officials denied rumors that President Fernando de la Rua would resign, the political climate remains tight as opposition Peronist Party governors adopt a belligerent stance against his government. \par \par \uc2  Traders said investors are still unsure of what level the real will steady at. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010912dx73006oj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
