\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Debt-Down amid Argentine economy, Brazil real woes. \b0\par\par\uc2  By Hugh Bronstein \par \uc2 562 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Juni 2001\par 18:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK, June 28 (Reuters) - Emerging market sovereign bond prices drifted slightly lower on Thursday as investors looked for positive news to counter recent signs of weakness in the Argentine economy and nagging worry about Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  "The market is a little weaker today because there are no positive developments and we do not see real money stepping in at these levels to support prices," said Owi Ruivivar, fixed income strategist at BNP Paribas. \par \par \uc2  Emerging market bond spreads widened by three basis points to 746 over U.S. Treasuries, according to J.P. Morgan's Emerging Markets Bond Index Plus. Argentina's portion of the index widened seven basis points to 1,003 while Brazil spreads remained flat at 845. \par \par \uc2  Wider spreads reflect the perception of increased risk as measured against safe-haven U.S. Treasury bonds. \par \par \uc2  "The market is trading off of the negative developments that have accumulated over the last week, such as the inefficacy of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2  and disappointing retail sales data from Argentina," Ruivivar said. \par \par \uc2  On Wednesday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, carrying out four emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the wilting real, which ended nearly one percent stronger. \par \par \uc2  Argentina supermarket sales fell 2 percent in May versus the same month in 2000 and May construction activity fell 1.1 percent year-on-year, Economy Ministry data shows. \par \par \uc2  Argentina's new global bond due 2008 fell a half point to bid 77.8, while the country's FRB paper shed 1/8 point to bid 83-3/4. \par \par \uc2  "Argentine FRB bonds are very vulnerable right now due to a deterioration in Argentine fundamentals, as will be the new 2008s and 2018s," Ruivivar said. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the U.S. Federal Reserve on Wednesday cut U.S. interest rates a modest quarter-percentage point, slowing the pace of its aggressive rate-cutting campaign while signaling it remained ready to do more if needed. \par \par \uc2  "There might have been some people who were hoping for 50 basis points who took a bit of profit," emerging debt trader said. "If we would have seen a 50 basis point cut, our market might have taken a little relief from that and rallied." \par \par \uc2  VENEZUELA DIPS WITH OIL PRICES \par \par \uc2  Venezuelan DCB bonds dropped 3/8 to bid 83-3/8 while the country's spread widened four basis points to 842 on Thursday amid jitters in the oil market. The solvency of Venezuela, a major oil exporter, is seen by Wall Street as dependent on petroleum prices remaining high. \par \par \uc2  NYMEX crude oil futures extended losses early Thursday after plummeting Wednesday, amid growing worries that the weakening economy is cutting demand. \par \par \uc2  NYMEX August crude fell 39 cents to an early low of $25.22 a barrel, extending an overnight loss of 24 cents. On Wednesday, the contract plunged $1.37 and hit a 14-month low. \par \par \uc2  "We recommend a defensive position on Venezuela, Argentina and Brazil," Ruivivar said. "We continue to like Mexico." \par \par \uc2  Ratings agency Standard & Poor's has said it is considering raising Mexico to investment grade status thanks to the country's improving fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Ruivivar said her favorite Mexican bond is the global due 2019. "This is Mexico's cheapest dollar-priced bond and should attract good crossover investor activity," she said. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6s00ok0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
