\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real firms after CenBank  \highlight22\uc2 interventions \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 315 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 23:50\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, June 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's beleaguered real \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  firmed on Wednesday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  aggressively \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, carrying out four emergency \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prop up the wilting real, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real clawed its way back to end at 2.305 reais per dollar, 0.95 percent stronger than at Tuesday's close of 2.327 reais. In morning trading, the real slipped to 2.337 reais. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it carried out two emergency sales of dollar-linked notes worth a total of 4 billion reais ($1.7 billion). \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank also entered the market twice to sell dollars and shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  only confirms such \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  later in the day and never says exactly what it did. \par \par \uc2  "The supply of dollars has dried up in the market and people are testing the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to see if its disposition to flood the market with \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 ...is indeed true," said Mario Barristel, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  at Novacao brokerage. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga last week said the bank would adopt a more aggressive attitude to protect the real from speculative attacks. The bank said it was building a war chest of $10.8 billion of reserves to shore up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  That came after the real tumbled to a low of 2.48 reais to the dollar, off 27 percent since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  The bank also raised interest rates to stave off inflationary pressures ensuing from the real's slide. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been battered in past months as investors have pulled out of real-denominated assets on concern over Argentina's financial crisis and a chronic energy shortage in Brazil. \par \par \uc2  At the end of Wednesday, the real was off 18 percent since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6r00sk9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
