\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  By Selling Dlrs - Traders \b0\par\par\uc2 339 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 20:03\par \uc2  Capital Markets Report \par \uc2 CM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- The Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  came to the real's rescue for the second time Wednesday, this time selling dollars directly to banks in an attempt to prop up the sagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The real reacted immediately, moving to BRR2.316 to the dollar from an intraday low of BRR2.338. A trader who bought dollars from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told Dow Jones Newswires that the price was BRR2.315, the same as Monday, the last time the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At around 1820 GMT, the real was changing hands at BRR2.311, the strongest level of the day. Tuesday's close was BRR2.326 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The previous attempt to halt the real's decline earlier in the day by selling BRR1 billion worth of short-term dollar-indexed bonds failed, leading the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  to a second \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Investors bought the entire lot of dollar-indexed bills, but the real didn't bounce back. \par \par \uc2  This is the third direct \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling dollars since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  unveiled a package of measures Thursday to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At around 1840 GMT, the real was at BRR2.32 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's real came under pressure Tuesday following a three-session rally after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  didn't \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market despite a slight depreciation of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Investors got nervous and started to test the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new policy of active \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's initiative helped the real bounce back from a historic low of BRR2.48 to the dollar June 19, analysts are skeptical that the move will help the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  get any stronger. \par \par \uc2  There is still concern that Brazil may have trouble financing its balance of payments this year and next as political jitters and an energy crisis threaten to knock down foreign direct investments in the country by half. \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3145-1481; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument cm00000020010710dx6r00sdv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
