\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Real Ends Stronger As Ctrl Bk  \highlight22\uc2 Intervenes \highlight\uc2  4 Times \b0\par\par\uc2 539 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juni 2001\par 23:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real finished 0.9% stronger Wednesday thanks to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on four occasions. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  salvaged the ailing real by twice selling dollars on the market and twice offering dollar-indexed debt. \par \par \uc2  The first double whammy combination of dollar and debt selling failed to help the real after it hit an intraday low of BRR2.338 to the dollar, forcing the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to wade in again as part of its new hands-on approach to keeping the real's decline in check. \par \par \uc2  Second time round, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  helped revive the real by selling debt and dollars again, and it closed at BRR2.305 - its strongest point of the session. This compares with Tuesday's finish of BRR2.326. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold undisclosed sums of dollars into the market, while managing to sell all of its dollar-indexed debt on offer. First time round, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold a total BRR1 billion. On the second occasion, officials held an emergency auction and sold all BRR3 billion in dollar-indexed bills due August 2002. The maturity is one year shorter than the BRR1 billion worth of dollar-linked bonds that were sold earlier in the day. \par \par \uc2  It was the third session in which the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars on the spot market since Thursday's announcement of a package of measures to boost the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which has lost 15% of its value since the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  "It's too early to say whether the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has won or lost this battle," said Fabio Fukuda, analyst with Tendencias Consultoria Integrada in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  "Right now the market is looking for equilibrium and trying to position in relation to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new hands-on policy." \par \par \uc2  "If the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sticks to its firm stance, as it did today, I see room for the real to get stronger than the BRR2.30 level. Of course, this will also depend on capital inflows and the external scenario," he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders noted that this week marks the end of the first half of the year, and Friday is the expiration day of dollar futures - two events that add volatility to trading and may mask the true impact of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new policy of active \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to fight investors' need for dollars as there is much concern about Brazil's fundamentals. \par \par \uc2  Even though the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  increased interest rates by 150 basis points to 18.25% last week and unveiled a set of measures to boost international reserves and secure the payment of foreign liabilities, market participants said Brazil's widening current account deficit remains a source of concern. \par \par \uc2  Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it forecast a widening in the current account deficit to $26.5 billion, or 4.97% of gross domestic product, compared with a previous prediction of $26.3 billion. \par \par \uc2  Also, the market continues to be worried about Brasilia's political outlook, a local power crunch and troubled Argentina. \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires; 55-11-3145-1478;\par brazil@dowjones.com\par    (Adriana Arai contributed to this report.)\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020010711dx6r0135g\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
