\par\par \b \uc2  UPDATE 1- \highlight22\uc2 Brazil currency \highlight\uc2  firms on  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 259 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2001\par 23:43\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, June 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished stronger for a fourth session running on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to bolster the real's on-going recuperation from record lows, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real finished 0.6 percent stronger at 2.30 reais per dollar from Friday's close of 2.315. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold greenbacks after the real slipped to 2.32 earlier in the day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but, as usual, did not specify how. \par \par \uc2  "It's not that the market is in such a good mood, but that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears willing to guarantee a cheaper dollar (versus the real)," said a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pulled back from all-time lows last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by an aggressive 150 basis points on Wednesday. It followed that move with plans to raise a $10.8 billion war chest to bolster its foreign reserves and buttress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if need be. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's new aggressive stance helped reverse the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's snowballing depreciation. On Sunday, \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  President Arminio Fraga told newspaper Estado de S.Paulo the measures were a "break to put things in order." \par \par \uc2  Still, battered throughout this year by concern over neighboring Argentina, the state of the U.S. economy, local political scandals and a surprise energy shortage, the real is almost 18 percent weaker now than at the start of January. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6p00wnl\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
