\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real ends firmer after  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervenes \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 151 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Juni 2001\par 22:35\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, June 25 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished stronger for a fourth time in a row on Monday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold dollars to prop up the real's on-going recuperation, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real finished 0.6 percent stronger at 2.30 reais per dollar from Friday's close of 2.315. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold greenbacks after the real slipped to 2.32 earlier in the day. The \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market but, as usual, did not specify how. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has pulled back from all-time lows last week after the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised interest rates by an aggressive 150 basis points on Wednesday. It followed that move with plans to raise a $10.8 billion war chest to bolster its foreign reserves and buttress the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  if need be. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx6p00wfv\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
