\par\par \b \uc2  Emerging Mkt Stocks Charge Higher, Ignore US Weakness \b0\par\par\uc2 344 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 22 Juni 2001\par 17:31\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  NEW YORK -(Dow Jones)- Ignoring weakness in U.S. markets, emerging market shares were charging higher Friday. \par \par \uc2  Latin America's largest economy, Brazil, was showing the most encouraging results as continuing improvement of the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  provided it with momentum. The weak real had prompted a great deal of concern about interest rates and inflation there. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gained 2% in early trade Friday, however, adding to its 3.7% advance Thursday. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  this week hiked \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's key interest rate by 150 basis points and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The recent developments, as well as \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  head Arminio Fraga's determination to support the economy, have brought confidence back to Brazil. \par \par \uc2  Saying that Brazil was making "all the right moves," Bear Stearns Strategist Thierry Wizman raised his recommendation on the country's equities Friday to "overweight" from "cautious overweight." \par \par \uc2  Mexico, however, remains Bear Stearns' top pick, given Brazil's current energy shortage and its proximity to economically troubled Argentina. \par \par \uc2  Shares in Brazil's largest telecommunications company, Telemar (TNE), were surging 3.2% higher in healthy midday trade to $15.95. Simultaneously, financial group Unibanco (UBB) was rising 2.6% to $25.30. \par \par \uc2  In contrast, the Dow Jones Industrial Average was losing about 70 points late in the morning. \par \par \uc2  From Mexico, Spanish-language media giant Televisa (TV) was up 1.1% to $39.90, and beverage group Femsa (FMX) - maker of Dos Equis - was gaining 1.8% to $43.45 in light trade. \par \par \uc2  Among emerging Asian shares, South Korea's SK Telecom (SKM) was up 3.4% to $18.36 to match advances in its local shares overnight. The mobile telecommunications operator is wrapping up plans to buy back about 4% of its total shares by the end of June. The buyback aims to raise share prices amid ongoing talks to sell up to 15% of the company to Japan's NTT DoCoMo. \par \par \uc2  -By Amy Guthrie, Dow Jones Newswires; 201-938-2225; amy.guthrie@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1836 5076 \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6m02txs\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
