\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Seen Setting New  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\uc2  Rules-Analysts \b0\par\par\uc2 127 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2001\par 16:10\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Speculation mounted Thursday among local market players that Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will unveil a new set of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign-exchange intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policies, soon following a dramatic weakening of the real (BRR) in recent days. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Arminio Fraga called a press conference earlier Thursday for 1400 GMT to talk about "the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's action and the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ." The bank's press office wouldn't provide additional details. \par \par \uc2  The possible announcement is expected to come less than 14 hours after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's monetary policy committee decided to raise interest rates by 150 basis points to 18.25%, the biggest increase since March 1999. \par \par \uc2  Economists were expecting a 50-basis-point hike. \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx6l02ppy\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
