\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil Intervenes \highlight\uc2  To Strengthen Real;Sells Dlrs -Traders \b0\par\par\uc2 270 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 21 Juni 2001\par 17:28\par \uc2  Dow Jones Commodities Service \par \uc2 DJCS\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2 \f2 \par - - 21/06/01 15-28G\par \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par 1528GMT\par \f28 \par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO (Dow Jones)--\b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has just \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by selling dollars to prop up the country's weak real, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The size of the dollar sales couldn't be immediately determined by the primary dealers. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has a policy of not immediately commenting on \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  At 1535 GMT, shortly after the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the real was trading at BRR2.387 per dollar compared with BRR2.454 at the open. \par \par \uc2  On Monday, Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold $445 million on the spot market to prop up the real, after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  reacted negatively to Argentina's move to effectively devalue its peso for foreign trade deals. \par \par \uc2  Before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , comments from \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Governor Arminio Fraga lifted the real to BRR2.396 per dollar. Fraga spoke early Thursday about the planned introduction of a set of measures to boost Brazil's ability to fend off contagion from economically-troubled Argentina and the negative effects of an energy crisis. \par \par \uc2  Fraga's comments, combined with a larger-than-expected 150-basis-point hike in Brazil's basic interest rate to 18.25% late Wednesday, caused the real to strengthen from its closing level Wednesday of BRR2.468. \par \par \uc2  The real has lost about 21% of its value this year and driven up inflation amid worries about Argentina, as well as a 20% power rationing program and cracks in Brazil's five-party coalition government. \par \par \uc2  -By Terry Wade, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511.3145.1479; terry.wade@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument djcs000020010711dx6l012d5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw427\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal6405\pichgoal600
