e head Antonio Carlos Magalhaes would kick up a storm when he plans to resign Wednesday after being fingered for getting access to a secret senate vote list. \par \par \uc2  The fear is Magalhaes, a former presidential ally and kingmaker, has amassed a mountain of compromising material on several high-ranking politicians in his 50 years in politics. The other senator involved in the scandal quit Thursday. \par \par \uc2  Argentina was still on the market's radar as worries about fallout from the neighboring recession-hit economy despite the country releasing details of a confidence-building debt swap which would ease the country's risk of default. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010712dx5p02wzj\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
