\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Breaks 4-Day Losing Streak On  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 588 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 25 Mai 2001\par 22:28\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's real broke a four-session losing streak Friday after the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market to prop up the sagging \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Traders said the \b \highlight22\uc2 monetary authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold an undisclosed sum of dollars on the spot market as well as a BRR2 billion lot of dollar-indexed bonds to help boost the real, which has been persistently weak of late amid regional turmoil, local political jitters and a brimming energy crisis. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  reiterated it has a no-comment policy on direct \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Unlike Thursday's \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , today's move to sell dollars on the spot market made the real appreciate significantly from the historic low of BRR2.375 to the dollar and the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  finished at a midrate of BRR2.317 on a BRR2.315-BRR2.319 spread. That's stronger from Thursday's close of BRR2.348 to the dollar, its weakest point ever. \par \par \uc2  This marked the first time since mid-March that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to prop up the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  by selling U.S. greenbacks to investors. \par \par \uc2  "Our preliminary reading is that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is establishing a new \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  pattern, and maybe they'll have to pursue this strategy," said Octavio de Barros, chief economist with BBV Banco in Sao Paulo. \par \par \uc2  He noted, however, that there isn't much room for the real to appreciate in the near term amid the uncertainties that the energy crisis brings to Brazil's economic outlook. \par \par \uc2  Later, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  confirmed that it \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market by directly selling dollars to investors but didn't disclose the amount. \par \par \uc2  Even though investors are growing confident that troubled neighbor Argentina's plan to swap short-term debt for long-term bonds will go forward, the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been reacting to homegrown problems such as the energy crunch and political turbulence. \par \par \uc2  Economists have cut their growth forecast for Brazil to below 3% from 4% to 4.5% after the government unveiled a rationing plan that calls for a 20% reduction in electricity use during at least six months, beginning in June. \par \par \uc2  BBV Banco's Barros said it is still unclear how big will be the overall impact of the energy crisis on the country's balance of payments, noting nonetheless that foreign direct investment will certainly fall. \par \par \uc2  "Right now we have a $19 billion foreign direct investment forecast for 2001, but this is an optimistic scenario and we maybe have to revise it downward in the future," he said. His real estimate is BRR2.30 to the dollar by year end. \par \par \uc2  Brazil received $6.76 billion in foreign investment in production of goods and services locally between January and April, while the country's current account deficit was $8.33 billion in the period. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had a $24 billion forecast for FDI in 2001 but said it is currently revising its estimates. \par \par \uc2  The energy crisis is also widely expected to hit Brazilian President Fernando Henrique Cardoso's popularity hard, reducing the chances that he will be able to elect a nominated successor in the 2002 presidential elections. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the bank said Brazilian international reserves inched lower to $35.731 billion Thursday from $35.730 billion Wednesday. Daily reserve figures are available at the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Internet site with a one-day lag. \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's Web site: {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.bcb.gov.br/"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 www.bcb.gov.br}}}\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  -By Adriana Arai, Dow Jones Newswires; 5511-3813-1988; adriana.arai@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx5p003i3\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
