\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2 's Real Ends Stronger On Bond Auction  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 472 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 21:39\par \uc2  Emerging Markets Report \par \uc2 EM\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO -(Dow Jones)- Following two unscheduled sales of dollar-indexed bonds by the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the country's local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  managed to close slightly stronger Monday after threatening, at one point, to finish at an all-time low. \par \par \uc2  By the close, the real ended at a midrate of BRR2.119 per dollar on a spread of BRR2.118-BRR2.120, after weakening as much as BRR2.176 per dollar earlier in the session. The real closed Friday at a 24-month low of BRR2.129 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  The real has been hurt by concern that Argentina's austerity program, unveiled Friday, won't have enough support in Congress to be carried through, and that it won't revive an economy that has been in recession for three years. \par \par \uc2  "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's plan seems to have worked and has helped pull the real from the edge of a new historic low," said a Sao Paulo-based trader. \par \par \uc2  "But I think it's only delaying the inevitable, because it hasn't removed the market's primary source of concern - Argentina," he added. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the real would probably have finished at an all-time low if the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  hadn't decided to sell dollar-linked debt. By midsession, the real was threatening to finish at its weakest point since March 2, 1999, when it closed at BRR2.17 to the dollar. \par \par \uc2  Another trader, based in Rio de Janeiro, however, was more optimistic about the real's direction going forward. \par \par \uc2  "I think the real will strengthen further tomorrow because the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is offering market operators an opportunity to hedge their positions," he said. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  plans to hold a third auction Tuesday, and the trader said he thought this would help the real regain the BRR2.100 level and maintain its position below the key psychological barrier until the end of the week. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  tried to sell a total of BRR4 billion worth of six-month dollar-indexed bonds in two separate emergency auctions Monday. In the first, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  sold 47% of BRR2 billion worth of debt put on offer, and in the second the sales totaled just 1.5% of the BRR2 billion on offer. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  comes as concern mounts in the market that the depreciating real will lead to inflation and this threatens to undermine the country's economic recovery the country following the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's early 1999 devaluation. \par \par \uc2  Brazil uses an inflation-targeting program to guide its monetary policy. The government has a 4% target for the Broad Consumer Price Index, or IPCA, this year. It successfully met the 2000 IPCA goal of 6%. \par \par \uc2  -By Anthony Dovkants, Dow Jones Newswires;55-11-3813-1988; anthony.dovkants@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2  1156 1843 \par \par \uc2 Dokument em00000020010711dx3j002xo\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
