\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  Ctrl Bk To  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  In Real Only On Volatility \b0\par\par\uc2 217 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 21:41\par \uc2  Dow Jones International News \par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.\par \par \uc2  SANTIAGO -(Dow Jones)- \b \highlight22\uc2 Brazil\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will only \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to support the real at moments of "high volatility or liquidity problems," a \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said Saturday on the sidelines of a Deutsche Bank conference. \par \par \uc2  Brazil's real ended Friday at a midrate of BRR2.129 to the dollar, the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's lowest close in over two years. The \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been on a weakening trend on concern that neighboring Argentina may not emerge from a three-year recession anytime soon. \par \par \uc2  Daso Maranhao Coimbra, who heads the Brazilian \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's international reserves \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2  department, or DEPIN, also said the Bank is maintaining its 4% year-end inflation target for 2001 despite fears that inflation is climbing. \par \par \uc2  Meanwhile, the Bank's Director for International Affairs Daniel Gleizer said Saturday that the real's recent slump would have to continue for an extended period of time before the \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  implemented a mechanism to keep the real from slipping further. \par \par \uc2  Brazil, South America's largest economy, floated the real in 1999, causing fears other Latin American economies would have to devaluate their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well. \par \par \uc2  -By Tom Darin Liskey and Christen A. Jamar, Dow Jones Newswires; 562-460-8546; chile@dowjones.com \par \par \uc2 Dokument dji0000020010711dx3h017ap\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
