\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Brazil \highlight\uc2  real at 2-year low after failed  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 354 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2001\par 15:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2001 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  SAO PAULO, March 16 (Reuters) - The Brazilian real reached new two year lows at the open on Friday after \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the previous session failed to lift a weight of U.S. and Argentine jitters, traders said. \par \par \uc2  The real fell to 2.109 per dollar from Thursday's second lowest ever close of 2.097 per dollar. The only time the real closed lower than that since it was introduced in mid-1994 was when it ended at 2.17 per dollar on March 2, 1999. \par \par \uc2  The real's weakest intraday level is 2.220 per dollar on March 2, 1999, a couple of months after it was devalued amid an emerging market crisis. \par \par \uc2  "Some investors are looking for the (dollar) hedge and another part of the market is speculating," said Novacao head dealer Mario Battistel. "What's clear is that it's best to stay on the defensive." \par \par \uc2  Thursday's fall came despite \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  buying dollars during the afternoon. The Bank said it had bought three lots of dollars because the real had decoupled from the reality of Brazil's economy and was taking on a life of its own. \par \par \uc2  Traders said the bank acted too little too late and had given confidence to players who wanted to test the Bank's resolve to support the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  On Thursday the real suffered concerns about the U.S. economic slowdown, worries ahead of a keenly-awaited Argentine economic announcement on Friday, and an explosion on Brazilian state oil giant Petrobras' biggest oil platform. \par \par \uc2  The market is anxiously waiting for Argentina's recently appointed economy minister Ricardo Lopez Murphy to announce new measures to revive the moribund neighbouring economy. \par \par \uc2  Traders will have their eyes peeled for any indications of legislator support or opposition to his keenly awaited plan. \par \par \uc2  Despite the market turbulence Brazil's \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Friday that Brazil sold 80 billion yen ($650 million) of six-year Samurai bonds with a coupon rate of 4.75 percent. It last launched Samurais in late November with a 60 billion yen offering. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010713dx3g03ri0\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (brazil near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Datum\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 01/01/1995 bis 21/08/2023\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalph